# Mandatory TDD for development changes

**MANDATORY: Before writing or modifying production/implementation code, you MUST read and follow `.cursor/skills/tdd/SKILL.md` (the `/tdd` skill) in full.**

Treat every feature, bugfix, refactor that changes behavior, and API/surface change as a TDD task. Do not start implementation until you have loaded that skill and are executing its Red → Green → Refactor phases.

## When this applies

- New features or behavior
- Bug fixes
- Refactors that change observable behavior
- Changes to public APIs, hooks, components, or core packages

## When this does NOT apply

- Pure documentation (README, comments-only with no behavior change)
- Rule/skill/config edits that do not change app or package runtime behavior
- User explicitly says to skip TDD for this task

## Hard requirements (from `/tdd`)

1. Run baseline tests for the target module before edits
2. Write EXACTLY ONE failing test first; run it and capture the real failure output
3. Write only the minimal code to make that test pass; run tests again
4. Refactor only after green; re-run the module suite
5. NEVER write a test file and implementation in the same tool-call turn
6. NEVER assume pass/fail without running the test runner

This applies to YOU and to every subagent you spawn for development work. Include this rule and the path to `.cursor/skills/tdd/SKILL.md` in those subagent prompts.
